   "minutes": "0-7",
   "activity": "Teacher distributes the laundry log and reads it aloud with the class. Teacher sets the scene: a community washing yard recorded these five days. Without explaining anything, teacher asks: 'Look at Day 1 and Day 3. The clothes dried much faster on Day 3. What is different between those two days in the table?' Students observe silently for one minute, then two or three volunteers share initial observations. Teacher does not confirm or correct — this surfaces what students notice before structured work begins."
  },
