 "time_bands": [
  {
   "minutes": "0-7",
   "activity": "Teacher places the situation card in front of each pair and reads it aloud once: a flour-mill owner has a heap that is a mixture of wheat grains, small pebbles, loose husk, iron bolt fragments, and rainwater that has dissolved a spilled bag of salt into the heap. The question is simple and immediate: 'Before you plan anything, tell your partner every difference you can observe between any two things in this heap.' Pairs talk; teacher takes three or four responses aloud and writes the properties named on the board — size, weight relative to air, magnetic character, solubility in water, whether something is solid or dissolved — building the property column of the reference chart live."
