 ],
 "time_bands": [
  {
   "minutes": "0-7",
   "activity": "Teacher presents the rooftop garden setting with a brief verbal picture: a flat concrete roof in a city, midday sun, five complaints from the people who work and sit there. The five scenario cards are distributed face-down. Teacher reads card 1 aloud (metal pipes scalding to touch) and asks the class for an immediate, undefended guess: which chapter concept explains this? Responses are taken quickly without evaluation, establishing that the chapter's language is the toolkit for the session. Cards are turned face-up and groups begin."
