  {
   "minutes": "40-45",
   "activity": "Teacher draws a vertical line on the board creating two columns — left blank, right headed 'What the task needed'. Addressing the whole class: 'Tell me one thing you had to know to complete any part of this task.' As students name concepts — the three dimensions of health, communicable versus non-communicable, transmission routes, what a vaccine does, what a symptom versus a sign is, what a pathogen is, why lifestyle matters, what the AQI means — teacher writes each on the right side. When the list is complete, teacher draws a bracket around it and says: 'This list is the chapter. You just used it all at once on a village none of us had seen before — that is what the chapter is for.' No further summary is given."
  }
 ],
