   "minutes": "0-7",
   "activity": "Teacher distributes the river water data card and reads it aloud with the class. No labels or identities are given — only the six observations. Teacher asks: 'Before we classify anything, what does this sample seem to contain? List every distinct thing you think is present.' Groups write a first-pass inventory on their map template, naming as many components as the clues suggest. This surfaces prior knowledge and shows where groups are uncertain."
